      "faq": [
        {
          "q": "How do I find an Instagram reel I saw but didn't save?",
          "a": "Type the words you remember - a phrase from the caption, the product, the creator's name - and search. Results come back newest first, so if you saw it recently it should be near the top. Two or three distinctive words work far better than one common one."
        },
        {
          "q": "Can you reverse search an Instagram reel?",
          "a": "Not by video or image - no public tool can match a clip you're holding against Instagram's library. What works is searching the words attached to it: the caption, title, hashtags or the creator's name. That's what this tool does."
        },
        {
          "q": "Why is Instagram's own reels search so bad?",
          "a": "Instagram's search is built around accounts, hashtags and places rather than what a reel actually says, and it won't sort by date. This searches the indexed text of reels and orders by recency, so new reels surface immediately."
        },
        {
          "q": "Can I search reels by creator or hashtag?",
          "a": "Yes - a creator's name or a hashtag is just another keyword. Combine them with a topic word to narrow a busy niche."
